  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Math\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Math\n       Program: commons-math\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/Math.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-math.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 106\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Math-42\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\nf656676e3a9a9611c368d1da462ed0ce5c93308d\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2011-11-28 20:16:28 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nMATH-713\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MATH-713\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.math.optimization.linear.SimplexSolverTest::testMath713NegativeVariable\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.math.optimization.linear.SimplexTableau\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Negative value with restrictNonNegative\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nProblem: commons-math-2.2 SimplexSolver.\n\nA variable with 0 coefficient may be assigned a negative value nevertheless restrictToNonnegative flag in call:\nSimplexSolver.optimize(function, constraints, GoalType.MINIMIZE, true);\n\nFunction\n1 * x + 1 * y + 0\n\nConstraints:\n1 * x + 0 * y = 1\n\nResult:\nx = 1; y = -1;\n\nProbably variables with 0 coefficients are omitted at some point of computation and because of that the restrictions do not affect their values.\n\nComments:\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: Could you please check this against the latest development version from the subversion repository ?\nThere have been several fixes concerning these coefficients in simplex solver since 2.2\n\n[Micha\u0142 Skrzypczak]: I'm quite busy at work now... When I'll find some time, I'll try to test it. Of course I'd be glad if one of developers would do it before :)\n\n[Thomas Neidhart]: I have tested this problem with the latest trunk, and the problem still remains.\n\nThe attached patch handles the case of unconstrained variables that still occur in the objective function. I have also added a unit test.\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: Fixed in subversion repository as of r1207566.\n\nPatch applied directly.\n\nThanks to Michal for the report and thanks to Thomas for the patch.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.math.optimization.linear.SimplexTableau (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.math.optimization.linear.SimplexTableau (fixed)\n@@ -407,10 +407,12 @@\n             continue;\n           }\n           Integer basicRow = getBasicRow(colIndex);\n+          if (basicRow != null && basicRow == 0) {\n               // if the basic row is found to be the objective function row\n               // set the coefficient to 0 -> this case handles unconstrained \n               // variables that are still part of the objective function\n-          if (basicRows.contains(basicRow)) {\n+              coefficients[i] = 0;\n+          } else if (basicRows.contains(basicRow)) {\n               // if multiple variables can take a given value\n               // then we choose the first and set the rest equal to 0\n               coefficients[i] = 0 - (restrictToNonNegative ? 0 : mostNegative);"
}